      "title": "Most UK diplomats to leave East Jerusalem consulate, Israel says, as Miliband says 'vital services' to remain",
      "link": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cw33xd6vegnno?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "description": "Israel said in September it would act in response to UK sanctions on illegal Israeli settlements in the West Bank.",
      "source_name": "BBC World News",
      "published": "2026-10-08T15:21:46"
    },
    {
      "title": "Israel’s downgrading of UK consulate aims to tighten its hold on Jerusalem",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/08/israel-downgrading-uk-consulate-tighten-hold-jerusalem",
      "description": "<p>Consulate targeted in sanctions spat has unusual diplomatic status that clashes with Israel’s ambitions to fully annex the city</p><p>Israel’s attempt to close the British consulate general in Jerusalem was primarily designed to deter London from imposing sanctions on settlements in occupied Palestine. But it also served the current government’s ambitions to fully annex Jerusalem as a national capital, diplomatic and legal experts said.</p><p>The UK mission to the city has an unusual diplomatic status, which dates back to before the founding of the state of Israel, rooted in a vision of Jerusalem as a neutral enclave under international control.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/08/israel-downgrading-uk-consulate-tighten-hold-jerusalem\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-08T17:16:03"
    },
    {
      "title": "British consulate in East Jerusalem will stay open as UK mission, says Ed Miliband",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/08/uk-consulate-east-jerusalem-remain-open-uk-mission-ed-miliband",
      "description": "<p>UK and Israel back away from full diplomatic confrontation, though British presence in Palestine will be much reduced</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/oct/08/holborn-st-pancras-byelection-labour-greens-zack-polanski-uk-politics-live-news-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Israel and the UK have backed away from a full-scale diplomatic confrontation, with Britain announcing it is rebranding its consulate general ⁠building in ⁠East Jerusalem ​as a UK mission, a move that will result in UK diplomats leaving Israel, with only seven to remain in the building. Among those leaving is the consul general, Helen Winterton.</p><p>The change was forced on the UK by the Israeli government as punishment for the decision by the foreign secretary, Ed Miliband, last month <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/08/uk-accuses-israeli-terrorists-ethnic-cleansing-west-bank-government-backing\">to ban trade with illegal settlements</a> and introduce a tougher sanctions regime against those who aided the building of settlements. The UK is seeking to protect the two-state solution as the best means of ending the Israel-Palestine conflict.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/oct/08/uk-consulate-east-jerusalem-remain-open-uk-mission-ed-miliband\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-08T16:43:39"
    },
    {
